This paper investigates a particular category of double phase problems with singularities, characterized by certain growth conditions and variable exponents, on a complete Riemannian manifold. The problem at hand is represented by the equation $$-\operatorname{div}\left(\frac{\left(\left(\left|u\right|^{p_1(x)}+c_1(x)\right)^{q_1(x)-1}
\left|u\right|^{p_1(x)}+\left(\left|u\right|^{p_2(x)}+c_2(x)\right)^{q_2(x}-1}
\left|u\right|^{p_2(x)}\right)\nabla u}{\left|u\right|^{a(x)}}\right)=\lambda\frac{F(x,u)}{\left|u\right|^{a(x)}}$$ where $p_i(x)$ and $q_i(x)$ are variable exponents, $c_i(x)$ are positive functions, and $F(x,u)$ exhibits superlinear growth. The existence of multiple solutions to this equation is demonstrated under specific conditions.
